var Availabilities_DeleteAvailabilitySchemaJSON = `{"description":"Deletes an availability. DELETE /v1/{name=calendars/*/availabilities/*} Soft delete: it is marked deleted, disappears from List unless ` + "`" + `show_deleted` + "`" + ` is set, and is purged at ` + "`" + `expire_time` + "`" + `. Recover it with Undelete before then. Deleting one makes its range fall back to whatever other availabilities say, or to no constraint at all if it was the last -- which is more permissive, not less. That asymmetry is worth a confirmation step in any interface built on this. NOT_FOUND          no such availability ABORTED            etag does not match PERMISSION_DENIED  caller may not delete it","properties":{"name":{"description":"Name of the availability to delete.","pattern":"^calendars/[^/]+/availabilities/[^/]+$","type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"}`
