// MCP tool descriptors. Each pairs a schema with a tool name and description
// so that LLM clients can discover and invoke the underlying RPCs.
var (
	Availabilities_CreateAvailabilityTool   = newTool("availabilities-create_availability_v1", `Creates an availability. POST /v1/{parent=calendars/*}/availabilities body: the availability itself Server-assigned fields on the request body are ignored: `+"`"+`name`+"`"+`, `+"`"+`uid`+"`"+`, `+"`"+`etag`+"`"+` and the timestamps are set by the server regardless of what is sent. Supply `+"`"+`availability_id`+"`"+` to choose the final path segment. Note the polarity, RFC 7953 section 3.1 <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7953.html#section-3.1>: creating one declares its whole range **unavailable**, and each AvailablePeriod inside it carves out time that is not. An Availability with no periods is valid and means "never schedulable in this range". Not idempotent. Retrying after a timeout may create a second availability; supply `+"`"+`availability_id`+"`"+` if the caller needs retry safety. ALREADY_EXISTS     that availability_id is taken INVALID_ARGUMENT   a field violates its buf.validate constraint PERMISSION_DENIED  caller may not create here`, Availabilities_CreateAvailabilitySchemaJSON, Availabilities_CreateAvailabilityOutputSchemaJSON, nil, "", nil)
	Availabilities_DeleteAvailabilityTool   = newTool("availabilities-delete_availability_v1", `Deletes an availability. DELETE /v1/{name=calendars/*/availabilities/*} Soft delete: it is marked deleted, disappears from List unless `+"`"+`show_deleted`+"`"+` is set, and is purged at `+"`"+`expire_time`+"`"+`. Recover it with Undelete before then. Deleting one makes its range fall back to whatever other availabilities say, or to no constraint at all if it was the last -- which is more permissive, not less. That asymmetry is worth a confirmation step in any interface built on this. NOT_FOUND          no such availability ABORTED            etag does not match PERMISSION_DENIED  caller may not delete it`, Availabilities_DeleteAvailabilitySchemaJSON, Availabilities_DeleteAvailabilityOutputSchemaJSON, nil, "", nil)
	Availabilities_GetAvailabilityTool      = newTool("availabilities-get_availability_v1", `Retrieves one availability. GET /v1/{name=calendars/*/availabilities/*} Safe and idempotent. Read the `+"`"+`etag`+"`"+` here and pass it back on update or delete to make the write conditional. NOT_FOUND          no such availability, or it is soft-deleted and `+"`"+`show_deleted`+"`"+` was not set INVALID_ARGUMENT   name does not match calendars/*/availabilities/* PERMISSION_DENIED  caller may not read it`, Availabilities_GetAvailabilitySchemaJSON, Availabilities_GetAvailabilityOutputSchemaJSON, nil, "", nil)
	Availabilities_ListAvailabilitiesTool   = newTool("availabilities-list_availabilities_v1", `Lists a calendar's availabilities. GET /v1/{parent=calendars/*}/availabilities Paginated per AIP-158: pass `+"`"+`page_size`+"`"+` (defaults to 50, capped at 1000) and the `+"`"+`next_page_token`+"`"+` from the previous response. Page tokens are opaque and may expire; do not construct or store them. Overlap is permitted and expected -- a general working-week pattern and a one-off exception may both apply, and `+"`"+`priority`+"`"+` decides which wins, RFC 7953 section 3.1 <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7953.html#section-3.1>. This method returns them all; it does not resolve them. INVALID_ARGUMENT   malformed filter, or page_size out of range PERMISSION_DENIED  caller may not list this collection`, Availabilities_ListAvailabilitiesSchemaJSON, Availabilities_ListAvailabilitiesOutputSchemaJSON, nil, "", nil)
	Availabilities_UndeleteAvailabilityTool = newTool("availabilities-undelete_availability_v1", `Restores a soft-deleted availability. POST /v1/{name=calendars/*/availabilities/*}:undelete Valid only before `+"`"+`expire_time`+"`"+`; after that it is gone and this returns NOT_FOUND. NOT_FOUND          no such availability, or already purged ALREADY_EXISTS     the availability is not deleted PERMISSION_DENIED  caller may not restore it`, Availabilities_UndeleteAvailabilitySchemaJSON, Availabilities_UndeleteAvailabilityOutputSchemaJSON, nil, "", nil)
	Availabilities_UpdateAvailabilityTool   = newTool("availabilities-update_availability_v1", `Updates an availability. PATCH /v1/{availability.name=calendars/*/availabilities/*} body: the availability itself A partial update: only fields named in `+"`"+`update_mask`+"`"+` are written. An empty mask writes every mutable field, which will clear anything the caller left unset -- pass a mask unless that is the intent. `+"`"+`available_periods`+"`"+` is replaced wholesale when the mask names it, not merged: the periods are positional value objects with no identity of their own, so there is nothing to match an incoming one against. Idempotent. Pass the `+"`"+`etag`+"`"+` read from Get to make the write conditional. NOT_FOUND          no such availability ABORTED            etag does not match the stored resource INVALID_ARGUMENT   mask names an unknown or immutable field PERMISSION_DENIED  caller may not modify it`, Availabilities_UpdateAvailabilitySchemaJSON, Availabilities_UpdateAvailabilityOutputSchemaJSON, nil, "", nil)
)

